# Quadlet network for the rootless network keeper on the native rootless `podman` venue (issue #458,
# docs/podman.md): a network of the keeper's OWN, with nothing else ever on it.
#
# Installed with pi-dispatch-netns-keeper.container, while the egress policy is armed. Podman's generator turns it
# into pi-dispatch-netns-keeper-network.service, which the keeper's unit requires. Internal= gives it no route out
# and DisableDNS= no aardvark-dns entry, so the one container on it can reach nothing at all, not even the proxy:
# jobs live on their own per-job `--internal` networks, which have no route to this subnet.
#
# NEVER REMOVE IT. Measured on Podman 4.9.3: `podman network rm -f` of this network kills the keeper, and a `podman
# network prune` or `podman system prune` run while the keeper is stopped removes it (with the keeper running, both
# leave it). Either way the keeper's unit cannot start again while this network's unit stays `active` (it ran once and
# exited), until `systemctl --user reset-failed` and a restart of both units. Its name is outside every prefix a
# pi-dispatch sweep removes.

[Network]
NetworkName=pi-dispatch-netns-keeper
Internal=true
DisableDNS=true
